## Fix: StrapiImage Layout, Hobbies Click, and Missing Card Images
- Root cause 1: <picture> wrapper caused layout issues (stretched images, inline element in block containers)
  - <picture> is inline by default; inside containers with aspect-ratio it didn't fill properly
  - CSS targeting .class img didn't match because the class was directly on <img>
  - Fix: Changed StrapiImage to render plain <img> with srcset/sizes (semantically correct for responsive sizing)
- Root cause 2: Home hobbies click broken
  - home.ts looks for document.getElementById("home-avatar")
  - Rewritten Home.astro didn't pass id="home-avatar" to StrapiImage
  - Fix: Added id prop to StrapiImage component; passed id="home-avatar" from Home.astro
- Root cause 3: Blog cards showed placeholder instead of image
  - Test post has featuredImage: null but headerImage is populated
  - Cards only used featuredImage, so they fell back to placeholder
  - Fix: index.astro and posts.astro now map featuredImage: p.featuredImage || p.headerImage
  - Also populate headerImage in the Strapi query so it's available as fallback

## Fix: Revert Home/About/404 to Local Images; Fix Blog CSS with :global()
- Reverted Home.astro, About.astro, 404.astro back to Astro <Image> with local assets
  - User confirmed Strapi images caused stretching/deformation in these sections
  - Local Astro Image handles sizing correctly for avatars and static illustrations
- Kept blog images (cards and hero) using StrapiImage for CMS-managed content
- Root cause of stretched blog images: Astro scoped styles don't apply to child components
  - `.blog-card__image-img` selector in BlogCard.astro didn't match the <img> rendered by StrapiImage
  - Fix: Changed to `:global(.blog-card__image-img)` in BlogCard.astro, posts.astro, blog/[slug].astro
