## Fix: Separate Global CSS Rule for blog/[slug].astro Hero Image
- Root cause: `:global(.post-hero__image)` combined with `.post-hero__image-placeholder` in same CSS rule caused Astro to scope both selectors
- Result: `object-position: center` was not applied to the hero image, causing it to show the top portion only
- Fix: Separated `:global(.post-hero__image)` into its own CSS block in blog/[slug].astro
- Verified: Build outputs truly global CSS `.post-hero__image{object-fit:cover;object-position:center}`
- Hero image is now properly centered vertically in the 120px container

## Fix: Home Hobbies Avatar Swap Broken
- Root cause: Astro `<Image>` generates `<img>` with `srcset` and `sizes` for responsive images
- When `bindHobbyListeners` changed `src` via JavaScript, the browser continued using the original `srcset`
- Result: avatar image never visually changed on click despite `src` being updated
- Fix: Added `avatarImg.removeAttribute("srcset")` and `avatarImg.removeAttribute("sizes")` before setting new `src`
  - Applied in both the swap-to-hobby and swap-back-to-default paths
  - File: `src/utils/home.ts` in `triggerSwap` function
- Verified: clicking "correr", "leer", or "videojuegos" now correctly swaps the avatar image
- 30 test files, 160 tests passing, 0 lint errors
- Build: 6 pages generated + 12 optimized WebP images

## MIG-025: Render Markdown Content in Blog Posts
- Root cause: Strapi stores blog post `content` as Markdown, but `blog/[slug].astro` rendered it raw via `set:html`
- Result: Markdown syntax (`# Title`, `**bold**`, etc.) appeared as plain text instead of rendered HTML
- Fix: Installed `marked` package and imported it in `src/pages/blog/[slug].astro`
  - Parse `post.content` with `marked.parse()` server-side before rendering and embedding
  - Parse `otherPost.content` for the embedded JSON used in client-side language switching
  - Both initial render and embedded data now contain HTML instead of raw Markdown
- Added comprehensive Markdown CSS styles in `blog/[slug].astro`
  - Headings (h1–h6), lists (ul/ol), links, blockquotes, code blocks, inline code
  - Tables, horizontal rules, strong/emphasis
  - Responsive font sizes for desktop breakpoint
- Verified: `/blog/test-post` now renders `<p>`, `<h1>`, etc. in dist HTML instead of raw Markdown
- 30 test files, 160 tests passing, 0 lint errors
- Build: 6 pages generated + 12 optimized WebP images

## MIG-026: Add Shiki Syntax Highlighting for Code Blocks
- Root cause: `marked` alone renders code blocks as plain `<pre><code>` without syntax highlighting
- Result: code snippets in blog posts appeared as monochrome text
- Fix: Installed `shiki` and `marked-shiki` packages
  - Created `Marked` instance with `markedShiki` plugin using `createHighlighter`
  - Theme: `github-dark`; languages: javascript, typescript, css, html, bash, json, markdown
  - `marked.parse()` now returns HTML with `<pre class="shiki github-dark">` and colored spans
  - Both `post.content` and `otherPost.content` parsed with Shiki highlighting
- Added Shiki-specific CSS in `blog/[slug].astro`
  - `pre.shiki`: padding, border-radius, `Fira Code` font, overflow-x auto, shadow
  - `code:not(pre code)`: inline code styling with accent background and color
- Verified: dist HTML contains `<pre class="shiki github-dark" style="background-color:#24292e">` with colored spans
- 30 test files, 160 tests passing, 0 lint errors
- Build: 6 pages generated + 12 optimized WebP images

