## Fix: Category Theme Leaking Between Pages
- Root cause: `data-category-theme` was set directly on `<html>` in `BaseLayout.astro`
- With `ClientRouter`, the `<html>` element persists across page swaps, so the theme from a blog post (e.g. `tech`) stayed active when navigating back to the home page
- Fix: Removed `data-category-theme` from `<html>` in `BaseLayout.astro`
  - Added a `<meta name="category-theme">` tag instead
  - Added an inline script that reads the meta tag and syncs `document.documentElement.dataset.categoryTheme` on initial load and after every `astro:after-swap`
  - When the meta tag is absent (e.g. home page), the attribute is deleted from `<html>`
- Verified: navigating from post → home no longer leaves a stale theme color

## Fix: Safari Mobile Menu Navigation Broken
- Root cause: `closeMobileMenu()` was bound directly to `click` on mobile nav links
- On Safari, removing the overlay immediately cancels the navigation before the browser follows the `<a href>`
- Fix: Updated `src/utils/mobile-menu.ts`
  - Nav links now only close the menu immediately for same-page anchors (`href="#..."`)
  - For cross-page links, the menu is closed in `astro:after-swap` instead
  - This gives Safari (and all browsers) time to process the navigation without interference
  - Also prevents stale `overflow-hidden` and overlay states after navigation
- Verified: mobile menu links now work reliably in Safari

## Fix: Theme Flash During ClientRouter Navigation (Safari)
- Root cause: `astro:after-swap` fires AFTER the new page content is already visible
- Result: brief flash of light theme when the user has dark mode selected
- Fix: Added `astro:before-swap` listener in `BaseLayout.astro`
  - Pre-applies the stored theme to `event.newDocument.documentElement` BEFORE the swap happens
  - The incoming page already has the correct `dark` class when it becomes visible
  - Kept `astro:after-swap` as fallback for edge cases
- **User verified:** no more theme flash when navigating between pages in Safari

## Fix: Mobile Menu Not Closing on Cross-Page Nav
- Root cause: previous fix only closed menu for anchor links (`href="#id"`)
- Result: clicking a nav link to another page left the mobile menu open
- Fix: Reverted to closing the menu for ALL nav link clicks
  - Used `requestAnimationFrame(closeMobileMenu)` instead of immediate call
  - `requestAnimationFrame` defers by one paint frame, giving Safari time to process the click
  - Avoids the `setTimeout(..., 50)` delay that caused stale states previously
- **User verified:** menu closes reliably for both same-page anchors and cross-page links

